# Production checklist
# 1. `.env` is NOT deployed with git — set variables in Vercel (or copy `.env` to a VPS).
# 2. Vercel blocks Gmail SMTP — use Resend (Option 2) for production.
# 3. Start locally with: npm run start
#
# Option 1 — Gmail SMTP (works locally; NOT on Vercel)
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=mamenkooo@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS="your16chargmailapppassword"
SMTP_FROM=Payka Orders <mamenkooo@gmail.com>
ORDER_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL=mamenkooo@gmail.com

# Option 2 — Resend (recommended for Vercel)
# Setup: https://resend.com → Sign up → API Keys → Create API Key
# 1. Copy the key (starts with re_) — shown only once.
# 2. For testing, use RESEND_FROM below (sends only to your Resend account email).
# 3. For production, verify your domain at resend.com/domains and use orders@yourdomain.com
# 4. When RESEND_API_KEY is set, the app uses Resend instead of Gmail SMTP.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxx
# RESEND_FROM=Payka Orders <onboarding@resend.dev>
# ORDER_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL=payka.jwlr@gmail.com

# Google Sheets — each order is appended as a new row
# Paste scripts/google-apps-script-orders.js into the sheet's Apps Script editor,
# deploy it as a web app, then put the URL and the same secret here.
GOOGLE_SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL=
GOOGLE_SHEETS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Vercel workaround — send emails via Google Apps Script + Gmail (no SMTP, no custom domain)
# Requires GOOGLE_SHEETS_* above. Redeploy the Apps Script after updating it.
# Local dev: leave false and use Gmail SMTP instead.
# SEND_EMAIL_VIA_GOOGLE_SCRIPT=true
